From: Amphora <amphora@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] lavapipe: resolve Android ANB layout for deferred (aliased) swapchain images

When Android's libvulkan.so performs deferred gralloc buffer binding via
vkBindImageMemory2 (VK_ANDROID_native_buffer), image->vk.android_buffer_type
is ANDROID_BUFFER_NATIVE_ALIAS rather than ANDROID_BUFFER_NATIVE.

lvp_bind_anb_memory() calls lvp_image_init() with the VkNativeBufferANDROID
struct attached to pCreateInfo, but lvp_image_init() only checked
vk_image_is_android_native_buffer(&image->vk). As a result, android_surface
remained false, llvmpipe allocated a 64px-aligned non-linear layout larger
than the linear gralloc buffer, and vk_android_import_anb() failed with
VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE ("failed to do deferred gralloc buffer bind").

Check vk_image_is_android_native_buffer_alias() as well so deferred ANB
images query vk_android_get_anb_layout() and import with the gralloc stride.
---
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/lavapipe/lvp_image.c
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/lavapipe/lvp_image.c
@@ -63,7 +63,8 @@
    /* This section is removed by the optimizer for non-ANDROID builds */
    VkImageDrmFormatModifierExplicitCreateInfoEXT eci;
    VkSubresourceLayout a_plane_layouts[LVP_MAX_PLANE_COUNT];
-   if (vk_image_is_android_native_buffer(&image->vk)) {
+   if (vk_image_is_android_native_buffer(&image->vk) ||
+       vk_image_is_android_native_buffer_alias(&image->vk)) {
       VkResult result = vk_android_get_anb_layout(
          pCreateInfo, &eci, a_plane_layouts, LVP_MAX_PLANE_COUNT);
       if (result != VK_SUCCESS)
